# Feasibility-test working files (prototype scripts, sample CSVs, converted photos)
# stay local -- they were throwaway and still are.
#
# ONE exception: STATUS.md is committed. It is the full test log -- what was tried,
# what the result was, and which conclusions were later struck -- and it is the only
# record of any of that. Note the glob: git will not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so the exclusion has to be on the contents for the negation to apply.
pipeline-test-artifacts/*
!pipeline-test-artifacts/STATUS.md

# Real photos: raw human uploads and the script's processed output.
# Never commit actual location photos to the repo.
incoming/
processed/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Generated by plan_sync.py --write-merge-csv; regenerate, never edit by hand.
merge.csv

# LibreOffice lock files. Created beside a spreadsheet while it is OPEN and
# removed on close, so one appearing in `git status` means a CSV is open right
# now -- and that any unsaved edits in it are NOT in your next commit.
.~lock.*#
